<%# locals: (mcp_url:) %>
<%# How a leader connects ChatGPT to Edify (#402), after the Claude guide, which covers what an assistant can see and
    the Handbook. Steps follow OpenAI's "Add custom MCP server" guide; custom servers are on some ChatGPT plans only. %>
<div class="card mb-5" id="connect_chatgpt">
  <div class="card-header">
    <h4>Connect ChatGPT</h4>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <p>
      ChatGPT can answer the same questions from Edify and sees the same information as Claude. It connects on ChatGPT
      on the web, on plans that allow custom MCP servers. If you don't see the option, your plan doesn't include it.
    </p>

    <ol>
      <li>In ChatGPT on the web, open <strong>Plugins</strong>, select <strong>+</strong>, then <strong>Add custom MCP server</strong>.</li>
      <li>Name it <strong>Edify</strong> and enter this server URL:</li>
    </ol>
    <%= render partial: "settings/connected_apps/copyable", locals: { text: mcp_url } %>
    <ol start="3">
      <li>Choose <strong>OAuth</strong> for authentication, review the warning, and select <strong>Create as a plugin</strong>.</li>
      <li>Install it, sign in to Edify if asked, and choose <strong>Allow</strong>.</li>
    </ol>

    <p>
      On a ChatGPT Free, Plus or Pro plan, OpenAI may use your conversations to improve its models unless you turn off
      <strong>Improve the model for everyone</strong> under <strong>Settings &gt; Data controls</strong> in ChatGPT.
    </p>

    <p class="mb-0">
      To stop ChatGPT's access, disconnect it below. It loses access at once.
    </p>
  </div>
</div>
